 "final_passage": "On the Halvard-Parl English→Estonian test set, Tessaline achieved a higher mean BLEU than Varrow-NMT (28.4 ± 0.6 vs. 27.6 ± 0.8), a statistically significant mean paired difference of 0.8 BLEU points (paired t-test, p = 0.017, 95% CI [0.2, 1.44]). Tessaline also substantially outperformed the PhraseGrid baseline in BLEU, with a statistically significant mean paired difference of 6.35 points (paired t-test, p < 0.001, 95% CI [5.87, 6.83]). Tessaline showed higher mean chrF than both Varrow-NMT and PhraseGrid (58.1 ± 0.8 vs. 57.7 ± 0.5 and 52.4 ± 0.5, respectively), although no statistical test was reported for these chrF differences.",
